{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T15:45:01.917Z","event":"test-critique","id":"WS-11","findings":[{"severity":"major","category":"test-quality","subject":"Schedule provisioning coverage","message":"No scheduler test appears in the diff, despite two new schedules and an explicitly required `infra/scheduler.test.ts`. A plausible implementation with no schedules, wrong intervals, the wrong queue/role, or malformed payloads would pass the changed tests. Add resource-construction tests for both schedules, their rates, ScheduledTaskQueue ARN, execution role ARN, and payload parsing with `scheduledTaskMessageSchema`.","evidence":[{"kind":"location","file":"infra/scheduler.ts","startLine":48},{"kind":"concern","named":"the diff adds createSchedules and SCHEDULE_DEFINITIONS but contains no infra/scheduler.test.ts diff"}],"workstreamId":"WS-11"},{"severity":"major","category":"test-quality","subject":"Notification URL deploy assertion","message":"The tests exercise only the exported pure comparison helper, not its use in `createInfra`. A wrong implementation could retain `assertSquareNotificationUrlMatches` solely for the tests while never registering the `$resolve(...).apply(...)` deploy-time assertion, and all shown tests would pass. Add a composition-level test that verifies createInfra installs the assertion and propagates a mismatch failure.","evidence":[{"kind":"location","file":"infra/queues.test.ts","startLine":296},{"kind":"location","file":"infra/index.ts","startLine":27},{"kind":"concern","named":"helper behavior is tested, but deploy-time wiring is not"}],"workstreamId":"WS-11"},{"severity":"major","category":"test-quality","subject":"Web configuration linkage","message":"The web tests assert only `WEB_ENV_MAPPING`; they do not construct `createWeb` and inspect its `link` and `environment` arguments. Omitting CartCookieSecret or AppBaseUrl from the actual Next.js function would still pass, although the acceptance criterion requires both mapping and linkage.","evidence":[{"kind":"location","file":"infra/secrets.test.ts","startLine":67},{"kind":"location","file":"infra/web.ts","startLine":36},{"kind":"concern","named":"no shown test invokes createWeb"}],"workstreamId":"WS-11"},{"severity":"major","category":"test-quality","subject":"Signature-failure alarm provisioning","message":"The alarm test checks source text and mostly truthy constants, not the CloudWatch resources or their composition into infrastructure. A wrong implementation that never calls `createSignatureFailureAlarm`, targets the wrong log group/topic, or builds an ineffective metric filter would pass. Instantiate the alarm with fakes and assert its metric filter, alarm configuration, action, and createInfra wiring.","evidence":[{"kind":"location","file":"infra/queues.test.ts","startLine":315},{"kind":"location","file":"infra/alarms.ts","startLine":69},{"kind":"concern","named":"assertions use source containment and truthiness rather than created alarm resources"}],"workstreamId":"WS-11"},{"severity":"minor","category":"test-quality","subject":"Webhook secret link coverage","message":"The webhook test verifies environment values but not the function's `link` array. A plausible implementation could expose the three values in `environment` while omitting the corresponding SST secret links, violating the declared linkage requirement. Assert all three Square secrets are linked to the HTTP function.","evidence":[{"kind":"location","file":"infra/queues.test.ts","startLine":213},{"kind":"location","file":"infra/queues.ts","startLine":237},{"kind":"concern","named":"test inspects environment only"}],"workstreamId":"WS-11"}]}
