{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T16:38:26.689Z","event":"test-critique","id":"WS-12","findings":[{"severity":"blocker","category":"test-quality","subject":"WS-12 end-to-end coverage","message":"The diff adds seed data and CI wiring, but contains no additions for `ordering.spec.ts`, `sandbox-fulfillment.spec.ts`, or the Square checkout interception fixture. Consequently, the required browse → child participant selection → cart subtotal → stubbed checkout journey, price-tamper rejection, production-stub refusal, and real sandbox fulfillment behavior are not backed by tests in this diff. A wrong or absent implementation of all of those behaviors would pass the shown changes.","evidence":[{"kind":"location","file":"apps/web/e2e/fixtures/seed.ts","startLine":76},{"kind":"concern","named":"The diff seeds ordering data but adds no corresponding Playwright spec files or Square-stub fixture."},{"kind":"location","file":".github/workflows/ci.yml","startLine":125}],"workstreamId":"WS-12"},{"severity":"blocker","category":"test-quality","subject":"Integration skip audit tests","message":"CI invokes `scripts/assert-integration-tests-ran.ts`, but neither that script nor tests proving its failure/pass behavior are included in the diff. The acceptance criteria require discriminating tests for skipped suites, executed suites, and an absent required suite. Without them, the audit can be incorrectly implemented—or not exist—and the CI change cannot establish that integration suites are protected from silent skipping.","evidence":[{"kind":"location","file":".github/workflows/ci.yml","startLine":103},{"kind":"location","file":"vitest.workspace.ts","startLine":36},{"kind":"concern","named":"The workspace comment references assert-integration-tests-ran.test.ts, but no such test or audit implementation is present in the diff."}],"workstreamId":"WS-12"},{"severity":"major","category":"test-quality","subject":"CI sandbox-test reporting","message":"The CI summary treats presence of `SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN` as proof that the sandbox fulfillment spec ran. That is not a discriminating assertion: the spec could be filtered out, skipped for another prerequisite, or execute zero tests while this step reports that it ran. Add a test/reporting mechanism that inspects Playwright results and explicitly verifies the sandbox spec's executed or skipped status.","evidence":[{"kind":"location","file":".github/workflows/ci.yml","startLine":128},{"kind":"concern","named":"The summary branches solely on SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN rather than on test execution results."}],"workstreamId":"WS-12"}]}
